  <h1>About Haldrecht</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Ramon Sanders — ISO 27001 readiness and internal audit.
  </p>

  <h2>Experience</h2>
  <p>
    I previously built integrated quality, safety and environmental management
    systems for small and mid-sized companies, as an adviser with a client
    portfolio. Every client taken through to external certification passed.
    That is earlier QHSE work, not an ISO 27001 reference for SaaS firms, and
    no client is named.
  </p>
  <p>
    Before that, the technical and regulatory side of industrial projects, and
    application and licence management in healthcare, where demonstrable
    control of access and contracts was the substance.
  </p>
  <p>
    I am studying business administration at the Open Universiteit, and I
    intend to study law after that. That is a study plan, not a practice.
  </p>

  <h2>Qualifications</h2>
  <p>
    ISO 9001 Lead Auditor (in progress). ISO 27001 Lead Auditor (in progress).
    CIPP/E (in progress). None of the three is presented here as held.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <p>
    I do not judge the statute and I do not use a protected title. I do not
    issue a certificate. Accredited certification bodies do that. I do not
    issue an accountant's report. I never certify my own work. The person who
    implements is never the internal auditor for the same client.
  </p>
  <p>
    An independent internal audit (not a certification audit) is a separate
    engagement from the implementation.
  </p>

